The differences in ranking scales between the two SD measures stem from differences in the "measurement units" of the original metrics. Ranks emphasize relative positions and are highly sensitive to small differences. In contrast, log2FC values, being continuous, are more influenced by absolute magnitudes, which often exhibit clustering.

Unfortunately, none of these plots highlight any particularly interesting genes. From the second plot, we also observe that the rank SD is very high for the vast majority of detected genes (which makes 1/SD_rank smaller). This underscores the need for a better method to account for rank SD, rather than relying on the average.

